  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v10.5.3 — BuiltIn constants, opt-in CORS, project website, Web UI fixes and performance. No breaking changes.\n\nNew — opt-in CORS for static browser clients. `Delibera:Server:Cors:AllowedOrigins` registers a named CORS policy listing the browser origins permitted to call the API cross-origin, and `UseCors` is wired only when that list is non-empty. Off by default: the Web UI reaches the API through its own same-origin BFF route and never needs CORS. Origins are matched exactly; there is no wildcard switch. `AllowCredentials` together with `*` is rejected at startup with a message naming the config key.\n\nNew — BuiltIn constants extracted across Delibera.Core. A single source of truth for HTTP headers, SSE event names, config sections, role names and other magic strings that previously drifted between projects. SSE event names remain a contract with the Web UI.\n\nFixed — three per-request costs on the server. ValidationFilter cached validator type resolution per argument type. RedisDebateOrchestrator now reuses the injected ConnectionMultiplexer instead of opening its own. The SSE writer assembles each frame once in the response pipe and flushes once, with event names as u8 literals.\n\nFixed — the proxy kept upstream SSE connections open after the browser left. The proxy now aborts its own fetch when the response closes before it was fully written.\n\nFixed — Web UI behaviours: cancel now distinguishes \"cancelled\" from \"already finished\"; changing a filter reloads from page 1; npm test now builds first via pretest so it passes on a clean checkout; the live view announces rounds to screen readers via a polite live region; every route titles itself; hover states and visible focus rings added.\n\nFixed — the Web UI typecheck was passing while silently checking less. Nuxt upgraded to 4.6.1, vue-router to ^5.4.0 matching it, vue-tsc to 3.3, vitest to 5, @nuxt/test-utils to 4. The check is clean for the first time.\n\nChanged — Node is pinned to an exact patch (22.23.3), because nuxt@4.6.1 declares engines.node: ^22.22.3 || ^24.15.0 || >=26.0.0.\n\nNew — GitHub Pages deploys the project website (Next.js static export in site/), not the Web UI. The site reads the version from Delibera.Core.csproj at build time, renders docs at any depth, and serves release notes, measurements, and debate templates extracted from source.\n\nCI — Docker Hub publish is now behind an environment (dockerhub-prod), like NuGet (nuget-prod). Release workflow creates the GitHub Release page from docs/WhatsNew-*.md. Merge commits are used instead of squash so ancestry checks remain meaningful.\n\nTests: Core + Server + gRPC tests passing, plus Web UI tests (API contract + SSE streaming). Clean under -warnaserror.",
